  "summands_3": {
    "note": "m=3 uses the chained Semaev system (two S_3 with a full-field intermediate U). Observations: (1) symmetry breaking (nb_break, GGMP 3.1) raises the decomposable fraction toward 3!=6 at 131-shape; (2) the chained refutation degree D* is structure-independent (=5 across subfield/standard/random at n=8 dim2 and n=9 dim2), because the full-field intermediate U dilutes the factor base structure. The special-subspace degree drop (HKY) lives in the DIRECT symmetric S_4 encoding, not in chaining, and that encoding needs more variables than the dense Macaulay instrument handles. The m=2 direct results already show the special-subspace effect (subfield/standard below random).",
